{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/15/codegen_prompts/5.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/15`\n- 题号：`5`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/15/5.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"5\">\n- `description`：将每个面板中的\"种子\"像素按照面板边框颜色指定的生长规则扩展为特定形状的图案。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格被 Grey 分隔线分为 2x2 共 4 个面板。\n  - 每个面板由不同颜色的一像素厚边框围成（如 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow）。\n  - 每个面板内部有一个 Magenta 的单像素\"种子\"。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - Red 边框面板：种子向四个正交方向各生长 2 像素，形成十字形，使用 Magenta 颜色。\n  - Blue 边框面板：种子向四个对角方向各生长 2 像素，形成 X 形，使用 Magenta 颜色。\n  - Green 边框面板：种子扩展为一个 3x3 的实心方块，使用 Magenta 颜色。\n  - Yellow 边框面板：种子保持为单像素不变。\n  - 生长超出面板内部边界的部分被裁剪。\n\n- `Key insight`：边框颜色是生长规则的选择器——每种颜色对应一种固定的扩展模式；解题者需要从样例中归纳出颜色到生长模式的映射表。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/581f7754, train/8a6d367c, train/e9fc42f2, eval/dbff022c, train/c920a713, eval/2c181942, train/c803e39c, train/aa62e3f4\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3773\nmechanism=0.4312\nlexical=0.0204\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:axis, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3735\nmechanism=0.4375\nlexical=0.0198\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:frame, object:marker, object:sprite, object:square, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8a6d367c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8a6d367c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"upper colored template mask s\",\n  \"dst\": \"rectangular frame interior d containing partial fill-color seed pixels\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"block-scaled s contains all seed pixels in d\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear dst to bg and paint the full matched scaled mask with the seed color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to the rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e9fc42f2\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3432\nmechanism=0.3815\nlexical=0.0189\ncode_feature=0.6667\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e9fc42f2.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e9fc42f2.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAssemble the foreground objects by docking equal-colored boundary markers edge-to-edge.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has a dominant background color and several 4-connected multicolor foreground\nobjects.  One foreground color is the body color; the less frequent foreground colors are\nboundary connector markers, and each marker color appears once as a free end or twice as a\nmatched docking pair.\n\nRule\nCrop each foreground object to its bounding box and translate the objects so that the two\noccurrences of every paired connector color touch on their exposed boundary sides.  Preserve\neach object's orientation and colors, then return the tight crop around the assembled\nforeground on the original background color.\n\nKey insight\nThe colored marker pixels are ports: matching colors specify which objects must touch, and\nthe marker's side of its object determines the direction of the translation.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"4-connected foreground object sprite s with boundary connector markers\",\n  \"dst\": \"matching boundary connector marker d on another sprite\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.marker.color and the two marker pixels have opposite exposed sides\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate sprites so each paired marker touches edge-to-edge; preserve sprite colors and orientation\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"tight crop of the assembled foreground on the original background color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3201\nmechanism=0.3243\nlexical=0.0178\ncode_feature=0.8000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c920a713\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3270\nmechanism=0.4049\nlexical=0.0182\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:output_resize, object:axis, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, object:square, operation:crop_resize, output:crop, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/c920a713.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/c920a713.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nUntangle overlapping colored rectangular frames into concentric square frames ordered by their visible crossings.\n\nInput structure\n- The background contains several one-cell-thick axis-aligned rectangular frames, one color per frame.\n- Frames overlap, and the visible color at an overlap records a directed crossing from the hidden frame to the visible frame.\n- Each foreground color still has visible pixels on the perimeter of its full rectangular bounding box.\n\nRule\n- Infer each color's full rectangular frame from the bounding box of its visible pixels.\n- Add a directed edge A -> B when B is visible at a crossing of A and B's frame perimeters.\n- Find the unique path that visits every frame color once, then render those colors as one-pixel-thick concentric square frames from outside to inside.\n\nKey insight\n- The output is not a crop of the input; the crossing graph gives a single frame order, and that order is redrawn as nested rings.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"overlapping one-cell-thick rectangular frames on the background\",\n  \"dst\": \"concentric square frame layers from outermost to innermost\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"rank(s.color in the unique directed crossing path) == rank(d from outermost to innermost)\",\n  \"transform\": \"reconstruct each frame from its visible-pixel bbox; add A->B when B is visible at a crossing of the two frame perimeters; redraw each ordered color as one nested one-cell-thick ring\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"square of side 2N-1, where N is the number of frame colors\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2c181942\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3202\nmechanism=0.3897\nlexical=0.0191\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:output_resize, object:axis, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, object:square, relation:direction, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/2c181942.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/2c181942.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAttach monochrome sprites to the matching sides of a central hollow square.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
